<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:15:20Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Is Iran headed to war or peace after Mecca alliance meeting?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac69c226afde442037838f4bdf00755a2ed2f7de8ff28738fe19855bf63595b4</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-iran-headed-to-war-or-peace-after-mecca-alliance-meeting/a-79788256--9ef674df50a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-iran-headed-to-war-or-peace-after-mecca-alliance-meeting/a-79788256?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia, Pakistan and Turkey have taken their latest peace push directly to Tehran. Officially, it was to avert a new military escalation, but their diplomatic outreach can also be seen as a warning to Iran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU's 'Made in Europe' push unnerves global auto suppliers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a57dfdada279f7d67e5511c74e1270b0b65b88633a701ad1aef3a87796bef87</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:15:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-s-made-in-europe-push-unnerves-global-auto-suppliers/a-79732579--7391c1bc1a80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-s-made-in-europe-push-unnerves-global-auto-suppliers/a-79732579?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In shielding Europe's carmakers from Chinese rivals, the EU risks hurting close partners from Turkey and Morocco to Japan and South Korea. Billions in trade and hundreds of thousands of European jobs are at stake.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Russia in Africa: What is Putin hoping to achieve?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d5b18fa8442021fca9f74678ac0078112e10763e5ec2e337bc613bbf26d83ab</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T09:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-in-africa-what-is-putin-hoping-to-achieve/a-79781858--24074440aebf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-in-africa-what-is-putin-hoping-to-achieve/a-79781858?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following its invasion of Ukraine and the resulting rift with the West, Russia has declared that it intends to make a "historic return" to Africa. What have we seen of this so far?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbian police shoot dead assailant at Israeli Embassy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1c4673fd37524af231f85d5927304336aa7b18d36611a1fd7d8628696addd9e</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:15:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T08:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbian-police-shoot-dead-assailant-at-israeli-embassy/a-79782905--d152a4aa69fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbian-police-shoot-dead-assailant-at-israeli-embassy/a-79782905?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A "minor" has been killed by police after attacking a guard at Israel's embassy in Belgrade with knives, the interior minister says. Ivica Dacic said police had declared the highest terror alert after the incident.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar: Is the US undermining the EU's diplomatic blockade?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aae640ab10896233bf70cba46eb9513bff4ed4eced9df5ecf2d655e2f8cc0ab5</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T15:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-is-the-us-undermining-the-eu-s-diplomatic-blockade/a-79778863--db2dea3e5776.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-is-the-us-undermining-the-eu-s-diplomatic-blockade/a-79778863?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With the US reopening talks with Myanmar's military-backed government, and several Southeast Asian countries restarting diplomatic contacts, the EU is facing uncomfortable questions about its own boycott of the junta.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Will elections in Israel change its Iran approach?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09767188b943a49baac4190f8ff36f1b31a4141bae75af10d0d2857792ae636c</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122--d46c291154a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Israelis head to the polls, the country's conflict with Iran casts a long shadow over the ballot box. But any leadership changes in Israel may not be enough to shake up its grand strategy on Tehran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A bad omen? Syria bans women from university courses</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3918fd2c0edb30fb440c5b9c7d06d3f98453a59600c256e6a475457a8f159ac6</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T20:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-bad-omen-syria-bans-women-from-university-courses/a-79769348--ba55f3eb7dc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-bad-omen-syria-bans-women-from-university-courses/a-79769348?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The recent announcement that Syrian tertiary institutes will not allow women into some courses has triggered debate. Critics worry it may be a sign that the new Syrian government is restricting women's rights.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why Ukraine may be involved in Mali's conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:988efd43528c2be9adf42912984d3ba19438ffb1d743016b3b776e40697c046e</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-ukraine-may-be-involved-in-mali-s-conflict/a-79743423--7ee87f683a22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-ukraine-may-be-involved-in-mali-s-conflict/a-79743423?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Allegations that Ukrainian specialists are supporting Tuareg rebels in Mali highlight Kyiv's effort to challenge Russian influence far beyond the battlefield in Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Merz in Asia as security issues loom large</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a42975ce424c1886ce8dd8828bdf850a88ac11c8559d0ab12570cea616117ad</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-in-asia-as-security-issues-loom-large/a-79764065--009b584587c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-in-asia-as-security-issues-loom-large/a-79764065?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz will be meeting the leaders of Singapore, Japan and South Korea as Germany seeks to adjust its foreign policy to rising uncertainty and threats to global supply chains.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Venezuelan opposition leader Machado returns from exile</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa73605bfa955abd6503389d0